<aetgt:getResponse xmlns:aetgt="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/repository/2010/10/avrepository.xsd"
                   xmlns:types1="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/repository/2010/10/avrepository.xsd">
   <types1:Item>
      <types1:EntryId>oEAVR3aaa-gt-16489539-2026-07-27T17:44:00.323Z::pd.xml</types1:EntryId>
      <types1:Name>Prcs_Dayforce_CPD</types1:Name>
      <types1:MimeType>application/xml+process</types1:MimeType>
      <types1:Description>Orchestrator: Dayforce to CPD employee integration (Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0)</types1:Description>
      <types1:AppliesTo/>
      <types1:Tags/>
      <types1:VersionLabel>2.0</types1:VersionLabel>
      <types1:State>CURRENT</types1:State>
      <types1:ProcessGroup/>
      <types1:CreatedBy>abdul.mannuru@hubbard.com.dev</types1:CreatedBy>
      <types1:CreationDate>2026-07-27T17:44:00Z</types1:CreationDate>
      <types1:ModifiedBy/>
      <types1:PublicationStatus>unpublished</types1:PublicationStatus>
      <types1:Entry>
         <process xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2010/10/avosScreenflow.xsd"
                  xmlns:tfm="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd"
                  xmlns:list="urn:activevos:spi:list:functions"
                  GUID="9YzFkZEq4V5kJlHTF4U0gK"
                  displayName="Prcs_Dayforce_CPD"
                  name="Prcs_Dayforce_CPD"
                  overrideAPIName="false">
            <parameterSet xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd">
               <parameter name="LastRunTimestamp" direction="in" type="string" description="Timestamp of the previous successful scheduled run. Empty on first run. See notes re: persistence."/>
               <parameter name="CurrentRunTimestamp" direction="out" type="string" description="Persist this as next run's LastRunTimestamp"/>
            </parameterSet>
            <appliesTo/>
            <description>Keeps CPD's person, contract, and phone records synchronized with Dayforce on a near-real-time basis, using an idempotent search-then-create-or-update pattern (Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0, section 2). Scheduled every ~15 minutes per build guide 4.16.</description>
            <tags/>
            <generator>Informatica Process Designer 11</generator>
            <notes>Hand-authored against the CPD-Dayforce Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0. See README_IICS_BUILD_NOTES.md at the repo root for: the XML-schema caveats that apply to every process in this build (this file has only ever been validated against one genuinely trivial start/end example, not a populated one - re-verify all node types in Process Designer before deploying); the full Open Items list carried over from the design doc (CPD hostname, VINCI ID EmployeeProperties XRefCode, org-unit cross-reference table, phone type code mapping, CPD auth mechanism, error-alert recipients); and operational notes on LastRunTimestamp persistence and the Schedule object (build guide 4.16), which lives in IICS Administrator and is not part of this export package.

Sequencing note vs. the build guide: step 4.15/step 3 lists "invoke GetEmployeeDetail_Process and SearchPerson_Process" without specifying order. This build calls GetEmployeeDetail_Process first and feeds its EmployeeNumber into SearchPerson_Process, since the sample Dayforce payload shows XRefCode and EmployeeNumber are the same value in practice, and SearchPerson_Process's Ext Id match needs EmployeeNumber - fetching detail first also avoids a wasted CPD search call if the Dayforce detail call itself fails.

CPD auth note: no Dayforce-style "Get token" action exists for CPD in cnctr_cpd_get because the design doc leaves the CPD auth mechanism unconfirmed (section 4.1). cpd_token below is sourced from a process input parameter (backed by a secure/connection parameter) until that is confirmed; if CPD turns out to need its own OAuth call, add a "Get CPD Token" action to cnctr_cpd_get mirroring the Dayforce pattern and call it here alongside inv-dftoken.</notes>
            <deployment skipIfRunning="false" suspendOnFault="false" tracingLevel="none">
               <rest/>
            </deployment>
            <extData>
               <nvpair name="treatEmptyStringAsNotNull">false</nvpair>
               <nvpair name="treatEmptyObjectListAsArray">true</nvpair>
            </extData>
            <flow id="df5ea9605-7f87-4c9c-bdfa-7d93f49d3ba0">
               <start id="k15f60530-72d4-4eb9-983a-b124a497eacf">
                  <link id="xl01" targetId="inv-getchanged"/>
               </start>

               <!-- Step 1 (build guide 4.15): pull the delta list of changed Dayforce employees -->
               <invokeProcess id="inv-getchanged" process="GetChangedEmployees_Process" title="Get changed employees">
                  <inputMapping>
                     <map source="LastRunTimestamp" target="LastRunTimestamp"/>
                  </inputMapping>
                  <outputMapping>
                     <map source="ChangedXRefCodes" target="ChangedXRefCodes"/>
                     <map source="CurrentRunTimestamp" target="CurrentRunTimestamp"/>
                  </outputMapping>
                  <link id="xl02" targetId="inv-dftoken"/>
               </invokeProcess>

               <!-- One Dayforce token acquired for the whole run and reused per employee, instead of once per employee -->
               <invoke id="inv-dftoken" connector="cnctr-test-dayforce" action="Get token" title="Get Dayforce token (run-scoped)">
                  <inputMapping>
                     <map source="processParameter:DayforceUsername" target="df_username"/>
                     <map source="processParameter:DayforcePassword" target="df_password"/>
                  </inputMapping>
                  <outputMapping>
                     <map source="access_token" target="access_token"/>
                  </outputMapping>
                  <link id="xl03" targetId="loop-employees"/>
               </invoke>

               <!-- Step 2 (build guide 4.15): loop over each changed employee -->
               <forEach id="loop-employees" collection="ChangedXRefCodes" item="XRefCode" title="For each changed employee">
                  <flow id="body-employee">
                     <start id="body-start">
                        <link id="bl01" targetId="scope-employee"/>
                     </start>

                     <!-- Step 6 (build guide 4.15/4.12): wrap the whole per-employee body in a fault handler -->
                     <scope id="scope-employee" title="Per-employee processing (fault-wrapped, build guide 4.13)">
                        <flow id="inner-employee">
                           <start id="inner-start">
                              <link id="il01" targetId="inv-getdetail"/>
                           </start>

                           <!-- Step 3 (build guide 4.15): get full employee detail -->
                           <invokeProcess id="inv-getdetail" process="GetEmployeeDetail_Process" title="Get employee detail">
                              <inputMapping>
                                 <map source="XRefCode" target="XRefCode"/>
                                 <map source="access_token" target="access_token"/>
                              </inputMapping>
                              <outputMapping>
                                 <map source="Employee" target="Employee"/>
                                 <map source="WorkContracts" target="WorkContracts"/>
                                 <map source="Contacts" target="Contacts"/>
                              </outputMapping>
                              <link id="il02" targetId="inv-search"/>
                           </invokeProcess>

                           <!-- Step 3 continued: search CPD for an existing match (see sequencing note above) -->
                           <invokeProcess id="inv-search" process="SearchPerson_Process" title="Search CPD for existing person">
                              <inputMapping>
                                 <map source="Employee.EmployeeNumber" target="EmployeeNumber"/>
                                 <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                              </inputMapping>
                              <outputMapping>
                                 <map source="PersonFound" target="PersonFound"/>
                                 <map source="personVinciId" target="personVinciId"/>
                                 <map source="ExistingContractId" target="ExistingContractId"/>
                                 <map source="ExistingPhones" target="ExistingPhones"/>
                              </outputMapping>
                              <link id="il03" targetId="dec-createOrUpdate"/>
                           </invokeProcess>

                           <!-- Step 4 (build guide 4.7): Decision / router -->
                           <decision id="dec-createOrUpdate" title="Person found?">
                              <case condition="PersonFound = true" targetId="inv-update"/>
                              <case condition="PersonFound = false" targetId="inv-create"/>
                           </decision>

                           <!-- Scenario 2 (Update path, build guide 4.9) -->
                           <invokeProcess id="inv-update" process="UpdatePersonAndContract_Process" title="Update person + contract">
                              <inputMapping>
                                 <map source="Employee" target="Employee"/>
                                 <map source="WorkContracts" target="WorkContracts"/>
                                 <map source="personVinciId" target="personVinciId"/>
                                 <map source="ExistingContractId" target="ExistingContractId"/>
                                 <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                              </inputMapping>
                              <link id="il04" targetId="dp-resolveActiveIds"/>
                           </invokeProcess>

                           <!-- Scenario 1 (Create path, build guide 4.8) -->
                           <invokeProcess id="inv-create" process="CreatePersonAndContract_Process" title="Create person + contract">
                              <inputMapping>
                                 <map source="Employee" target="Employee"/>
                                 <map source="WorkContracts" target="WorkContracts"/>
                                 <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                              </inputMapping>
                              <outputMapping>
                                 <map source="NewPersonVinciId" target="NewPersonVinciId"/>
                                 <map source="NewContractId" target="NewContractId"/>
                              </outputMapping>
                              <link id="il05" targetId="inv-writeback"/>
                           </invokeProcess>

                           <!-- Scenario 4 (VINCI ID writeback, Create path only, build guide 4.10) -->
                           <invokeProcess id="inv-writeback" process="WriteVinciId_Process" title="Write VINCI ID back to Dayforce">
                              <inputMapping>
                                 <map source="XRefCode" target="XRefCode"/>
                                 <map source="NewPersonVinciId" target="NewPersonVinciId"/>
                                 <map source="access_token" target="access_token"/>
                              </inputMapping>
                              <link id="il06" targetId="dp-resolveActiveIds"/>
                           </invokeProcess>

                           <!-- Both branches converge here before phone reconciliation -->
                           <dataProcess id="dp-resolveActiveIds" title="Resolve active personVinciId/contractId for this run">
                              <description>Update path uses the ids returned by SearchPerson_Process; Create path uses the ids returned by CreatePersonAndContract_Process. Only one branch will have populated its variables, so the iif() falls through cleanly.</description>
                              <expression target="ActivePersonVinciId">iif(PersonFound, personVinciId, NewPersonVinciId)</expression>
                              <expression target="ActiveContractId">iif(PersonFound, ExistingContractId, NewContractId)</expression>
                              <link id="il07" targetId="dp-comparePhones"/>
                           </dataProcess>

                           <!-- Step 5 / Scenario 3 (build guide 4.11): compare phone lists -->
                           <dataProcess id="dp-comparePhones" title="Compare phone list (Dayforce vs. CPD)">
                              <description>OPEN ITEM: Contacts.Items field names (ContactType/ContactDetail below) and the Dayforce-contact-type-to-CPD-phoneTypeCode mapping are placeholders - the design doc leaves the phone type code mapping unconfirmed (section 3.2.5), and no sample of the expanded Contacts.Items shape was provided. mapPhoneType/parseDiallingCode/parseNumber represent lookup/parsing logic that still needs to be written once both are confirmed against a live expanded GetEmployeeDetail call. ExistingPhones may also come back empty from SearchPerson_Process today - see that process's notes.</description>
                              <expression target="DayforcePhones">list:project(Contacts, '{ phoneTypeCode: mapPhoneType(ContactType.XRefCode), diallingCode: parseDiallingCode(ContactDetail), number: parseNumber(ContactDetail) }')</expression>
                              <expression target="PhonesToAdd">list:where(DayforcePhones, 'not list:exists(ExistingPhones, "phoneTypeCode = " &amp;amp; phoneTypeCode)')</expression>
                              <expression target="PhonesToUpdate">list:where(DayforcePhones, 'list:exists(ExistingPhones, "phoneTypeCode = " &amp;amp; phoneTypeCode &amp;amp; " and number != " &amp;amp; number)')</expression>
                              <expression target="PhonesToDelete">list:where(ExistingPhones, 'not list:exists(DayforcePhones, "phoneTypeCode = " &amp;amp; phoneTypeCode)')</expression>
                              <link id="il08" targetId="loop-phonesToAdd"/>
                           </dataProcess>

                           <!-- Step 5 continued (build guide 4.12) -->
                           <forEach id="loop-phonesToAdd" collection="PhonesToAdd" item="Phone" title="For each phone to add">
                              <flow id="body-phoneadd">
                                 <start id="pa-start"><link id="pal1" targetId="inv-addphone"/></start>
                                 <invokeProcess id="inv-addphone" process="AddPhoneNumber_Process" title="Add phone">
                                    <inputMapping>
                                       <map source="ActivePersonVinciId" target="personVinciId"/>
                                       <map source="ActiveContractId" target="contractId"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.phoneTypeCode" target="phoneTypeCode"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.diallingCode" target="diallingCode"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.number" target="number"/>
                                       <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                                    </inputMapping>
                                    <link id="pal2" targetId="pa-end"/>
                                 </invokeProcess>
                                 <end id="pa-end"><title>End</title></end>
                              </flow>
                              <link id="il09" targetId="loop-phonesToUpdate"/>
                           </forEach>

                           <forEach id="loop-phonesToUpdate" collection="PhonesToUpdate" item="Phone" title="For each phone to update">
                              <flow id="body-phoneupdate">
                                 <start id="pu-start"><link id="pul1" targetId="inv-updatephone"/></start>
                                 <invokeProcess id="inv-updatephone" process="UpdatePhoneNumber_Process" title="Update phone">
                                    <inputMapping>
                                       <map source="ActivePersonVinciId" target="personVinciId"/>
                                       <map source="ActiveContractId" target="contractId"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.phoneTypeCode" target="phoneTypeCode"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.diallingCode" target="diallingCode"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.number" target="number"/>
                                       <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                                    </inputMapping>
                                    <link id="pul2" targetId="pu-end"/>
                                 </invokeProcess>
                                 <end id="pu-end"><title>End</title></end>
                              </flow>
                              <link id="il10" targetId="loop-phonesToDelete"/>
                           </forEach>

                           <forEach id="loop-phonesToDelete" collection="PhonesToDelete" item="Phone" title="For each phone to delete">
                              <flow id="body-phonedelete">
                                 <start id="pd-start"><link id="pdl1" targetId="inv-deletephone"/></start>
                                 <invokeProcess id="inv-deletephone" process="DeletePhoneNumber_Process" title="Delete phone">
                                    <inputMapping>
                                       <map source="ActivePersonVinciId" target="personVinciId"/>
                                       <map source="ActiveContractId" target="contractId"/>
                                       <map source="Phone.phoneTypeCode" target="phoneTypeCode"/>
                                       <map source="processParameter:CpdToken" target="cpd_token"/>
                                    </inputMapping>
                                    <link id="pdl2" targetId="pd-end"/>
                                 </invokeProcess>
                                 <end id="pd-end"><title>End</title></end>
                              </flow>
                              <link id="il11" targetId="inner-end"/>
                           </forEach>

                           <end id="inner-end">
                              <title>End</title>
                           </end>
                        </flow>

                        <!-- Step 6 continued (build guide 4.12-4.13): route any fault raised above to ErrorAlert_Process -->
                        <faultHandlers>
                           <catchAll>
                              <flow id="fault-flow">
                                 <start id="fault-start">
                                    <link id="fl01" targetId="inv-erroralert"/>
                                 </start>
                                 <invokeProcess id="inv-erroralert" process="ErrorAlert_Process" title="Send error alert">
                                    <inputMapping>
                                       <map source="XRefCode" target="XRefCode"/>
                                       <map source="fault:activityName" target="FailedStepName"/>
                                       <map source="fault:httpStatus" target="HttpStatus"/>
                                       <map source="fault:message" target="ErrorMessage"/>
                                    </inputMapping>
                                    <link id="fl02" targetId="fault-end"/>
                                 </invokeProcess>
                                 <end id="fault-end">
                                    <title>End</title>
                                 </end>
                              </flow>
                           </catchAll>
                        </faultHandlers>
                        <link id="bl02" targetId="body-end"/>
                     </scope>

                     <end id="body-end">
                        <title>End</title>
                     </end>
                  </flow>
                  <link id="xl04" targetId="end-l08f9dfc7-24cc-443b-93b1-cfe87135576c"/>
               </forEach>

               <end id="end-l08f9dfc7-24cc-443b-93b1-cfe87135576c">
                  <title>End</title>
               </end>
            </flow>
         </process>
      </types1:Entry>
      <types1:GUID>9YzFkZEq4V5kJlHTF4U0gK</types1:GUID>
      <types1:DisplayName>Prcs_Dayforce_CPD</types1:DisplayName>
   </types1:Item>
   <types1:CurrentServerDateTime>2026-07-27T17:46:15.07Z</types1:CurrentServerDateTime>
</aetgt:getResponse>
